630530,"position":"SF","lastName":"Murphy III","firstName":"Trey","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1631255,"position":"C","lastName":"Matković","firstName":"Karlo","status":"Confirmed"},{"personId":1642847,"position":"PG","lastName":"Fears","firstName":"Jeremiah","status":"Confirmed"}]},"reportModules":[{"moduleType":"game_header","order":0},{"moduleType":"defining_moments","order":1},{"moduleType":"top_performers","order":2},{"moduleType":"shot_difficulty","order":3},{"moduleType":"gravity_spotlight","order":4},{"moduleType":"defensive_spotlight","order":5},{"moduleType":"leverage_spotlight","order":6}],"gameOverview":{"title":"The New Orleans Pelicans Earn the Win","body":"The New Orleans Pelicans defeated the Memphis Grizzlies 135-134. Zion Williamson led New Orleans with 25 points, 11 rebounds and 4 assists on 9-for-15 shooting, while Karlo Matković added 25 points on 9-for-13 accuracy with 5 three-pointers made. Memphis countered with Ty Jerome's 40-point performance on 14-for-22 shooting and 5-for-6 from three, alongside 5 rebounds and 5 assists. Cameron Boozer contributed 18 points and 9 rebounds for the Grizzlies.\n\nThe Pelicans built momentum in the third quarter, going on a 19–6 run to establish control during that stretch. Memphis responded with an 11–0 run in the fourth quarter and into overtime, but New Orleans held firm down the final stretch. Zion Williamson's jump shot with 1:16 remaining in overtime made the score 133–129 in favor of the Pelicans. Jeremiah Fears was involved in the decisive sequence with 0:07.3 left, and New Orleans secured the one-point victory. The New Orleans Pelicans got more second-chance scoring than the Memphis Grizzlies.\n\nJerome's offensive impact extended beyond his scoring output. He shot 18.5 percentage points above expectation, converting at a rate significantly higher than an average NBA player would be expected to achieve on the same tracked opportunities. Trey Murphy III drew above-expected defensive pressure for New Orleans, recording Average Gravity of 14.6, while Jerome's Total Leverage of 6.8 reflected his overall contributions across multiple facets of the game for Memphis."}},"defining_moments":{"gameId":"0022600165","moduleType":"defining_moments","definingMoments":[{"guid":"81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053","rank":1,"title":"Jeremiah Fears Attempts the Free Throw","summary":"With 7.3 seconds left in overtime, Jeremiah Fears was involved in the play, and the Pelicans led 135–134.","category":"Scoring","eventNum":759,"largeHls":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053_hls_3500kbps_1280x720.m3u8","largeUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053_1280x720.mp4","playerId":1642847,"smallHls":"","smallUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053_320x180.mp4","mediumHls":"","mediumUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053_960x540.mp4","playListUrl":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053.m3u8","largeDuration":5183,"smallDuration":5183,"largeThumbnail":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053_1280x720.jpg","mediumDuration":5183,"smallThumbnail":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053_320x180.jpg","mediumThumbnail":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/759/81aa7aa6-8119-e7da-e3c0-65e06977f053_960x540.jpg"},{"guid":"eec1ec7d-0661-2b2f-4217-7122e3e06495","rank":2,"title":"Ty Jerome Finishes the Layup","summary":"Ty Jerome converted the driving layup, and the score was tied 133–133 with 18.8 seconds remaining in overtime.","category":"Scoring","eventNum":743,"largeHls":"https://videos.nba.com/nba/pbp/media/2026/11/02/0022600165/743/e